    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **284 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**. (The lone `ERROR GeneralExceptionHandler` line is an expected log from an escalation-handler test, not a failure.)\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented AUDIT logging for successful owner creation on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**New function step** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- Logs to a dedicated SLF4J logger named `AUDIT` at INFO level.\n- Records the authenticated user (via `SecurityContextHolder`), the new owner's id, and the membership number (computed with the existing `OwnerMapper.membershipNumber`, consistent with the response DTO).\n- Message format: `owner created user=acceptance-admin id=11 membershipNumber=11`.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond`, so it runs only after the owner is persisted (and thus has an id) and only on the success path \u2014 every successful creation, never a rejected one.\n\nThe `authorize:` composition already proves the Spring Security context propagates to OfficeFloor functions, so `SecurityContextHolder` correctly resolves the authenticated user (`acceptance-admin` under the test's `@WithMockUser`).",
